From: Harshit Gupta <39994376+arelyx@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 10:33:55 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 23/24] freedreno/xenos: faster transfers and partial resolves

- CPU (de)tiling copies 16-byte contiguous runs (8 for 1-byte texels) instead of
  one texel at a time.
- Resolve and restore only the batch's scissor bounds, in 8-pixel blocks (Xenos
  resolves keep the rectangle's x, y in the destination).
- Blit-based texture transfers on Xenos, limited by a new pipe cap
  (texture_transfer_blit_min_pixels) to >= 128x128 transfers of 4-byte texels:
  x11perf putimage500 29.9 -> 147/s, shmput500 32 -> 332/s, small uploads unchanged.

dEQP-GLES2 1-in-20 sample: 98.2%, no regressions against the full run.

Generated-by: LLM
